{
  "configuration_id": "config_003",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_009: multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, weighted fusion → 52.3% acc, 0.87 GPU-h), the most informative next step is to test whether multiprofile aggregation provides a meaningful gain over the single-profile baseline. config_003 is the minimal, controlled extension of config_009: it keeps the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000), image encoder (resnet50), and fusion strategy (weighted), changing only the profile setting from single to multi with avgpool aggregation. This isolates the effect of multiprofile aggregation, which is the single most impactful architectural axis in the remaining search space (the majority of untested configs are multiprofile). A positive result would justify investing subsequent experiments in optimizing within the multiprofile space (encoder upgrades, transformer aggregation, concat fusion); a null or negative result would redirect effort toward single-profile encoder improvements or modality ablations. Expected relative cost: moderately higher than config_009 (~1.0–1.3 GPU-h) due to processing multiple profiles and the avgpool aggregation step, but still well within the cheaper tier compared to ViT-L or transformer-aggregation configurations. This is the best use of experiment 2 because it reduces the largest source of uncertainty (single vs. multi profile) at low cost and directly shapes the exploitation strategy for the remaining 7 experiments."
}

